      585, 08007 Barcelona, Spain
abstract: >-
  Three offline interactive companions, including a source-bound PaperGraph,
  editable figures, derived-table arithmetic checks, and raw-observer reconstruction
  for genome editing readouts. Manuscript and supplement are private. The
  offline runner reconstructs target observers and a common coding-string
  witness from nine authentic FASTQ streams using eighteen frozen alignment
  tables. It verifies conditional finite-universe bounds, contrasts, withdrawal
  certificates and exact agreement with three preserved result objects. This
  computational replay does not calibrate molecular accuracy, execute fresh
  alignment or establish independent biological replication. The original
  biological experiments are attributable to Sousa et al. Code licensing is
  scoped in metadata/LICENSE_SCOPE.json; data and scientific text retain
  separate terms.
keywords:
  - "genome editing readouts"
  - "observability"
  - "partial identification"
  - "sequence correspondence"
  - "CFTR F508del"

repository-code: "https://github.com/FacundoFirmenich/crispr-observability"
